---
source: crates/spela/tests/cli.rs
expression: help.stdout()
---
Linux gaming optimization tool for NVIDIA GPUs: per-game profiles, DLSS and
Proton settings, DLL management with backups, and GPU and CPU tuning around
Steam launches.

To launch a game with its profile, set its Steam launch options to
`spela %command%`.

Usage: spela [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  scan        Scan Steam libraries for games and their DLLs
  list        List the games found in Steam libraries
  show        Show one game and its DLLs
  launch      Show what launching a game would do (dry run only)
  profile     Manage per-game profiles and All games
  config      Show or change spela's settings
  dll         Manage DLSS, XeSS and FSR DLLs: list, update, install, restore
  dlss        DLSS settings in a profile
  gpu         GPU information, profile settings and reset
  cpu         CPU information, profile settings, governor and SMT
  proton      Proton settings in a profile
  denylist    The anti-cheat deny list for DLL swaps
  tui         Open the interactive terminal UI
  completion  Print a shell completion script
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --version
          Print the version

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Print results as JSON (schema version 1)

      --demo
          Run on built-in fictional data. Your files are never written

      --log-level <LEVEL>
          Log level. Overrides SPELA_LOG
          
          [possible values: off, error, warn, info, debug, trace]

Exit codes:
  0  success
  1  failure
  2  usage error
  3  config or profile file invalid
  5  another spela holds the lock
  In wrapper mode (spela %command%), the game's own exit code.

Environment:
  SPELA_LOG  log filter, such as debug or spela=trace
  NO_COLOR   turn colour off
